  "note": "CR 406.3's sticky half: once a player may look at a card exiled face down, they may keep looking until it leaves exile, even if the instruction that allowed it no longer applies. bob takes each land with a Confiscate and holds it through his own priority, then alice's Aura Graft moves the Confiscate onto her Island and the land comes home. Having held the Windbrisk Heights the Vesuva copied, which exiled nothing, bob's Synthetic Blind Reclamation is offered the hidden card's pile (CR 406.4); having held the Vesuva whose hideaway exiled it, he is offered the card by name. Both legs end with alice controlling every land, so no live read of hideaway's control can tell them apart; the copied land is taken first, since the look the copy gives would otherwise already be recorded. Face-up cards in exile give each Reclamation a second candidate, so its target prompt is asked rather than bound.",
